title: Preserve Snowbridge v1 inbound liveness when the Asset Hub sovereign is empty

doc:
  - audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
    description: |
      Snowbridge v1 inbound messages now burn the teleported Asset Hub execution fee from the
      relayer's Bridge Hub account instead of requiring funds in the Asset Hub sovereign account
      on Bridge Hub. The Asset Hub sovereign reimburses the relayer best-effort for the burned fee
      plus delivery reward when it has enough reducible balance.

      This preserves the existing funded-sovereign economics while preventing an empty Asset Hub
      sovereign from stalling the Ethereum-to-Polkadot inbound channel. In the empty-sovereign case,
      the message is still processed and the nonce advances, but the relayer is not reimbursed.

crates:
  - name: snowbridge-pallet-inbound-queue
    bump: patch
    validate: false
  - name: bridge-hub-westend-runtime
    bump: patch
